                                                "example_id": "b0379f42-9035-4d65-8346-7600c666378a",
                                                "sense_id": "61187b4a-5be1-3610-90cb-31db003ebd9e",
                                                "text": "When Earth's last picture is painted, and the tubes are twisted and dried,/ When the oldest colors have faded, and the youngest critic has died,/ We shall rest, and, faith, we shall need it -- lie down for an aeon or two,/Till the Master of All Good Workmen shall put us to work anew."
